{"id":"ec4101a5-c5ab-467b-89fb-63228db9844f","body":"On main `a73b7a6ac3d`, signed local Checkout fixtures returned HTTP 409 after the original worker committed the business transaction but left its receipt processing. This occurred for immediate and delayed success, asynchronous failure, and expiry. The receipt guard itself behaved correctly.

Local review commit `6f8900156d631660ab417ac237a9c24290e2c963` on `codex/evo-61-addon-webhook-replay` routes matching terminal add-ons through the locked order finalizers. Asynchronous failure resolves the current Stripe session and checks its binding and order. Five signed recovery cases now acknowledge the reclaimed receipt, deduplicate the next delivery, and preserve stock, entitlements, payments and refund counts. A conflicting order and conflicting open Checkout remain unacknowledged. The rejecting Stripe fixture prevented external calls.

Passed 392 PostgreSQL tests, 2,733 server unit tests and 1,725 app unit tests, production and touched-spec TypeScript checks, formatting, lint (three existing warnings) and Knope. The branch is local. Publication and its remaining image, infrastructure and browser gates are pending. [Entire Trail 38](https://entire.com/gh/evorto-app/-/trails/38).","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-20T12:04:50.882Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-20T12:04:50.636Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"5de66975-4b30-495f-a21e-303534976d2d","name":"Lukas Heddendorp"},"onBehalfOf":null}

